// A `#write` fn is a name like any other (spec §10, Modules): an @fmt sees the writers its
// code could name (§13, Formatting, rule 4). lib/geo's api.ctx declares Size's, which code
// outside uses; Point's is hidden, so only lib/geo writes a Point with it. A writer's result
// is a bare `!`, whose errors are its sink's, so its declaration states no set (rule 5).
//# program: main.ctx lib/geo/api.ctx lib/geo/impl.ctx
//# stdout:
//| 3px
//| (1, 2) 4px

//# program: outside.ctx lib/geo/api.ctx lib/geo/impl.ctx
//# errors:
//| outside.ctx:5:34: error: @fmt has no writer of geo::Point to utf8::Builder(arena::Arena)
